    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d519-a4">

                <pb facs="0716" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg620"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Royal Decree.</hi>
                </head>
                <p>In accordance with the opinion of my council of ministers, and in virtue of the
                    power conferred upon my Government by article 89 of the constitution of the
                    monarchy, in the name of my august son, King Alfonso XIII, and as Queen Regent
                    of the Kingdom, I decree as follows:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Article I</hi>. The electoral law of June 26, 1890,
                    shall be promulgated and observed in the islands of Cuba and Porto Rico, with
                    the modifications that have been introduced in the text that follows this
                    decree, with a view to its adaptation to the conditions of those
                    territories.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Art. II</hi>. The regulations and other necessary
                    provisions for the execution of the present decree, which the Government shall
                    before the Cortes, shall be prepared by the ministry of the colonies.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Maria Cristina.</hi>
                </p>
                <p>The president of the council of ministers:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Praxedes Mateo Sagasta.</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">Done at the <placeName type="venue"
                            >Palace</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1897-11-25">this 25th day of November,
                            1897</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
